{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# 🌿 Regen Knowledge Commons Toolkit\n\n**Master overview canvas — 2026-05-15 stabilization draft**\n\n10 layers · Minimum Operating Kernel · Core Movement · 18 Cross-Cutting Principles\n\nThis canvas is the entry point for navigating the Toolkit's architecture. Open layer canvases for depth.","x":-400,"y":-1300,"width":800,"height":300,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"core-movement","type":"text","text":"## Core movement\n\n> **Discover → Understand → Connect → Compose → Specify → Implement → Learn → Evolve**\n\nA contributor does not need to walk every move. Many will only add resources, only explain a concept, only review claims, only maintain infrastructure.","x":-400,"y":-950,"width":800,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"core-sequence","type":"text","text":"## Core sequence\n\n> Ontology → Knowledge → Resources → Options → Deployment → Tracks → Implementation → Evolution\n\n*Infrastructure (L10) sits under the system, not in the workflow.*","x":-400,"y":-660,"width":800,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"kernel","type":"text","text":"## Minimum Operating Kernel (v0.1)\n\n5 working objects, enough for one useful contribution without grasping the whole system:\n\n| Object | Question |\n|---|---|\n| **Resource** | What exists? |\n| **Concept** | What does it mean? |\n| **Option** | What can be selected, adapted, combined? |\n| **Deployment** | What must be explicit before use? |\n| **Signal** | What happened, what changed, what needs attention? |","x":-1500,"y":-1100,"width":600,"height":420,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"distinctions","type":"text","text":"## 16 Critical Distinctions\n\nResource vs Concept · Source vs Source System · Ontology vs Encyclopedia · Resource Graph vs Encyclopedia · Encyclopedia vs Concept Ecology · Encyclopedia vs Option Library · Tool vs Option · Option vs Deployment · Track vs Deployment · Deployment vs Implementation · Implementation vs Pattern · Signal vs Conclusion · Type vs Tag · Claim vs Evidence · Polished vs Reviewed · AI-assisted vs Human-reviewed\n\n*Master doc §3.15 — the most important architectural move is preserving distinctions.*","x":900,"y":-1100,"width":600,"height":420,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"L1","type":"text","text":"## L1 — Ontology & Semantic Kernel\n\n**What kinds of things exist, and how do they relate?**\n\nTypes · relationships · metadata · classification · interoperability\n\nOwners: Matt + Rather + Luiz","x":-1500,"y":-400,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L2","type":"text","text":"## L2 — Knowledge Commons / Encyclopedia\n\n**What does this mean?**\n\nConcepts · frameworks · domains · comparisons · guides · anti-patterns · open questions\n\n14 core knowledge domains · 67 articles live\n\nOwner: Heenal","x":-900,"y":-400,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L3","type":"text","text":"## L3 — Resource Graph & Ecosystem Atlas\n\n**What exists in the world?**\n\nProjects · people · orgs · tools · protocols · datasets · maps · source systems · events · cases\n\n738 entries lifted · curation pending\n\nOwners: Brandon + curator (TBD)","x":-300,"y":-400,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L4","type":"text","text":"## L4 — Concept & Idea Ecology\n\n**Where did these ideas come from, and how do they relate?**\n\nLineages · paradigms · metaphors · tensions · 10 concept clusters · 15 distinctions\n\nOwner: Matt (likely; confirm)","x":300,"y":-400,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L5","type":"text","text":"## L5 — Option Library\n\n**What reusable choices are available?**\n\n9 categories: governance · coordination · org · funding · token · knowledge · impact · ops · experimentation\n\n5 cross-category compositions\n\nOwner: Luiz (currently)","x":900,"y":-400,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L6","type":"text","text":"## L6 — Deployment & Structural Integrity\n\n**What must be explicit before use?**\n\n6 minimum checks (decision · info · power · accountability · failure detection · fixed/configurable/experimental)\n\n6 high-risk areas\n\nOwners: Luiz + Durgadas (CSIS-informed)","x":-1500,"y":-100,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L7","type":"text","text":"## L7 — Tracks & Composition\n\n**What pathway should someone follow?**\n\n♻ Restored from earlier iteration\n\n10 core track candidates: Newcomer · Community · Local Node · Funding Round · Knowledge Commons · Governance · Environmental · Bioregional · AI-Garden · Implementation Reviewer\n\nOwner: Heenal (returning)","x":-900,"y":-100,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L8","type":"text","text":"## L8 — Implementation & Learning Memory\n\n**What actually happened?**\n\n9 record types (pilot · campaign · funding round · governance · local node · knowledge commons · ecological/MRV · workshop · failure case)\n\nBonfires substrate candidate\n\nOwner: Koi (candidate)","x":-300,"y":-100,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L9","type":"text","text":"## L9 — Evolution Layer\n\n**How does the commons update itself?**\n\nAdaptive loop: Signal → Sensemaking → Balance → Intervention → Integration → Memory\n\n10 signal types · 8 failure modes\n\nOwner: Koi (candidate)","x":300,"y":-100,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L10","type":"text","text":"## L10 — Infrastructure & Substrate\n\n⭐ **NEW layer in 2026-05-15 iteration**\n\n**What tools and technical foundations can support this?**\n\n12 substrate types · substrate-by-need mapping · public/private/internal boundaries\n\nOwner: Luiz (operator default)","x":900,"y":-100,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"crosscuts","type":"text","text":"## 18 Cross-Cutting Principles (§4)\n\n1. Provenance and source lineage · 2. Attribution and return paths · 3. Maturity and review state · 4. Public-use boundaries · 5. Claim-evidence discipline · 6. Review should scale with risk · 7. Regenerative obligation · 8. Consent, privacy, and representation · **9. Anti-extractive synthesis ⭐** · 10. Interoperability without forced uniformity · 11. Type / tag discipline · **12. Pattern humility ⭐** · 13. Local and ecological care · 14. AI-assisted but human-governed · 15. Infrastructure should serve workflows · **16. Living systems health ⭐** · **17. Compost, archive, and memory ⭐** · 18. Contribution should be legible\n\n⭐ = new in 2026-05-15 iteration","x":-1500,"y":250,"width":3000,"height":260,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"min-rule","type":"text","text":"## Minimum Structural Rule\n\n> **A layer should not absorb the function of another layer unless the interface is explicit.**\n\n- A raw link list ≠ Encyclopedia content\n- A concept page ≠ an Option entry\n- A funding mechanism ≠ a valid Deployment\n- A Track ≠ an Implementation\n- A Case ≠ a Pattern (too quickly)\n- A Signal ≠ a Conclusion\n- A tag ≠ an ontology type\n- AI synthesis ≠ reviewed knowledge","x":-1500,"y":600,"width":1000,"height":300,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"swarm","type":"text","text":"## Knowledge Commoning Swarm context\n\nThe Toolkit enters the OpenCivics Knowledge Commoning Swarm as a **contribution artifact**, not as universal architecture.\n\n6 contribution streams · 4 Swarm shared outputs (Map · Assembly Wizard · Instructional Guide · Component Index) · 6 functional affordances (Store · Contribute · Find · Govern · Connect · Evolve)\n\nPulse 1: 2026-05-09–10 (happened) · 2-month hackathon: ongoing","x":-400,"y":600,"width":1000,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"plan","type":"text","text":"## Integration plan\n\nSee [`docs/plans/master-doc-iteration-may-15-2026.md`](docs/plans/master-doc-iteration-may-15-2026.md) for the full Phase A–G plan.\n\nPhase A: Save + archive (✅ done 2026-05-15)\nPhase B: 10 per-layer docs (✅ done 2026-05-15)\nPhase C: 10 layer canvases (✅ done 2026-05-15)\nPhase D: This master canvas (✅ done 2026-05-15)\nPhase E: Structured refactor — Phase 3 from May 6 plan, against new iteration (next)\nPhase F: Repo development infrastructure (next)\nPhase G: Site implications (deferred)","x":650,"y":600,"width":850,"height":300,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"backlog","type":"text","text":"## 📋 TODO Backlog\n\n[`docs/BACKLOG.md`](docs/BACKLOG.md) is the triaged TODO surface — mirrors master doc §16 with status labels (`raw-note` · `needs-routing` · `needs-owner` · `candidate-integration` · `high-risk` · etc.) + the §16 routing table (what kind of item routes to what layer).\n\n**HEARTBEAT.md** = in-flight this cycle\n**BACKLOG.md** = triaged + parked\n**Master doc §16** = constitutional read (1,820 lines of canonical backlog material + routing rules + 'what to avoid' rules + suggested AI instructions)\n\n*Dashboard surfaces open count + top-priority items.*","x":-1500,"y":1250,"width":1500,"height":280,"color":"2"},
